// The holding layout — ONE session, and it IS the main loop.
//
// This layout is the single place that decides what the main loop actually runs. `SessionHost`
// deliberately does not know: it starts the session and probes that it is alive, and what lives
// inside is this file's business.
//
//   start:   zellij --layout <this file> --session main
//   reach:   zellij attach main
//   remote:  docker exec -it <container> zellij attach main
//
// WHY A SESSION AND NOT JUST A PROCESS
// The agent must not die when the connection does. Inside a session it survives detach, a dropped
// VPN, a closed laptop, a reboot of YOUR machine — none of those are events in its life. The way in
// becomes interchangeable, which is the property that makes remote access safe to lose.
//
// ONE session. A second one is a second AGENT with its own idea of where the work stands, both
// writing the same running thread — a split brain with no merge. Bounded side-work goes to a minion
// (see agentboot/minion.py): one errand, a generated brief, a result handed back here.

layout {
    // The main loop. Replace the command with your agent's entrypoint.
    //
    // The `exec` matters: without it the shell stays as the pane's process and the agent becomes a
    // child, so a crash leaves you looking at a live shell in a pane whose agent is gone — a green
    // light wired to nothing, in pane form.
    pane command="bash" {
        args "-lc" "exec ${AGENT_MAIN_LOOP:-bash}"
        name "main loop"
    }
}
